1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:03,230
In the ground-floor Region
Editor, select the Briefing room

2
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:05,369
polygon to open Region Properties.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,260
Review its Name, Room Type,
Color and Description.

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:14,460
Searchable in dispatch is checked, while
Dispatchable is clear in this example.

5
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:16,350
These are separate options.

6
00:00:16,729 --> 00:00:20,360
We will verify the search setting
through New Call, rather than assuming

7
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:22,260
both checkboxes mean the same thing.

8
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:25,920
Clear Searchable in dispatch
and select Save Region.

9
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:30,159
On New Call, open Indoor
Location and search for Briefing.

10
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:33,469
The returned search now
says No results found.

11
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:36,450
This removes the room from
that new selection search.

12
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,389
It has not deleted the underlying
floor plan or the room polygon.

13
00:00:40,619 --> 00:00:43,839
Return to the same room’s
properties, check Searchable

14
00:00:43,839 --> 00:00:45,480
in dispatch and save again.

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,580
Repeat the Indoor Location
search on New Call.

16
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:51,849
Briefing room now returns
as a selectable result.

17
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:54,770
Dispatchable remains
clear during this test.

18
00:00:55,179 --> 00:00:58,879
The actual returned option verifies
which setting controls this

19
00:00:58,879 --> 00:01:00,510
search in the recorded system.

20
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:03,360
Select Briefing room from Indoor Location.

21
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:06,660
Review the selected room
name before saving the call.

22
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,900
The outdoor location is separate.

23
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:14,150
This fictional exercise also enters
a latitude and longitude and uses Set

24
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:16,549
Pin on Map to place the outdoor marker.

25
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:20,119
Selecting an indoor room has
not automatically supplied

26
00:01:20,119 --> 00:01:21,420
those outdoor coordinates.

27
00:01:21,730 --> 00:01:25,029
Review the outdoor map and the
indoor reference together so

28
00:01:25,029 --> 00:01:27,269
responders have the intended context.

29
00:01:27,419 --> 00:01:30,699
After preparing the call
information, select Save as

30
00:01:30,699 --> 00:01:32,620
pending, do not dispatch yet.

31
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:37,469
The submit button still reads Create
and Dispatch Call, so verify that

32
00:01:37,469 --> 00:01:41,110
the pending checkbox is selected
before submitting this exercise.

33
00:01:41,509 --> 00:01:44,610
The returned Pending Calls
list contains the saved call.

34
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:47,390
Open View and confirm the Pending banner.

35
00:01:47,759 --> 00:01:51,409
Then use Update Call and
scroll back to Indoor Location.

36
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:53,489
Briefing room is still selected.

37
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,550
This checks the persisted reference
independently of the original form.

38
00:01:57,819 --> 00:02:00,930
The floor plan and selected
room are stored references.

39
00:02:01,309 --> 00:02:04,609
They do not establish who is
currently inside the room, track

40
00:02:04,609 --> 00:02:06,980
movement or confirm physical arrival.

41
00:02:07,369 --> 00:02:09,690
Keep that distinction
clear when briefing a crew.

42
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:14,589
A community paramedicine or mental health
team can use a reviewed coordination-room

43
00:02:14,589 --> 00:02:19,380
reference; search-and-rescue, security,
wildland support and industrial

44
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,669
teams can use equivalent named areas.

45
00:02:22,089 --> 00:02:25,059
Use verified local map
information and the appropriate

46
00:02:25,059 --> 00:02:26,790
live-location tools separately.

47
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:31,480
This exercise demonstrates room search
and a saved pending-call reference.
